#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""acp-dispatch — hand a slice to an agent through Paseo and get its report back (a shim, slim-down E6, 2026-11-06).

Shim: removed with tools/acp-run in the follow-up PR (docs/slim/PLAN.md E6, Wave 6). It keeps the dispatch
contract callers rely on (the report file, `.done`, the jobs record, the exit codes, the footer, the outcome record,
the load gate and the frontier admission) and launches through `paseo run`, or, for a restricted Claude run,
through `bin/review-launch` (the E8 review boundary, which outlives this shim).

    acp-dispatch <agent> --model M --kind KIND --name NAME (-p PROMPT | -f BRIEF) [-C DIR]
                 [--role advise|exec] [--frontier-reason TEXT] [--effort LEVEL]
                 [--task TASK | --out DIR] [--perm all|read-only|deny] [--timeout S] [--lead NAME]
                 [--detach [--no-wait] [--wait-timeout S]] [--dry-run] [--json] [--force]
                 [--min-headroom PCT] [--est-pct PCT] [--load-wait SECONDS | --no-load-gate]
    acp-dispatch footer --report PATH [--lead NAME]   the shared footer, filled in, for an Agent-tool prompt
    acp-dispatch check (PATH)...                       classify reports, jobs/<name>.json records or out dirs
    acp-dispatch wait RECORD [--timeout S]             `paseo wait` on the slice, then classify (exit codes below)
    acp-dispatch tell RECORD MESSAGE [--from NAME]     inbox entry + `paseo send --no-wait --json` (MESSAGE - = stdin)
    acp-dispatch outcome RECORD [--ci pass|fail] [--review pass|fail] [--merged|--not-merged]

Retired with the shim (exit 2 naming the replacement): resume, reroute, auto-resume, extend, finalize, reap
(--install/--uninstall), cursor-cloud (bin/cursor-cloud stays: run it directly), --checkpoint, --no-preflight,
--no-auto-resume, --acp-arg, --context, --wrapup-grace, --no-model-check, --acp-run.

Agents are Paseo providers: claude, codex, antigravity, cursor, opencode, hermes, omp, grok (same name); any other
exits 2 with that list. `--model M` becomes `--provider P/M`. `--mode` is always passed (Claude's default is `auto`,
so no mode would not be read-only):
    --perm all        the provider's `defaultMode` from `paseo provider ls --json` (enabled and available, else 2)
    --perm read-only  claude: `bin/review-launch --mode read-only` (Read, Grep, Glob, WebFetch, WebSearch; empty
                      settings, MCP and hooks; bypass refused; tripwire 77). Other providers: a provider mode
                      (codex `read-only`; any other provider is refused, exit 2) that is VERIFIED at launch: the
                      agent is created with that mode and a no-op first prompt, `paseo agent mode ID --list` and
                      `paseo inspect ID` must show it listed and active, else the agent is stopped and the launch
                      refused (exit 2); only then is the brief sent. Provider-mode strength, WEAKER than review-launch:
                      no tool allowlist, no MCP or settings stripping, no tripwire.
    --perm deny       claude: `bin/review-launch --mode review` (Read, Grep, Glob, no network). Others: refused (2).
The record says which (`boundary`: review-launch | paseo-mode | paseo).

Launch: `load-watch admit --wait S --json --max-agents` first (exit 75 when too hot; --load-wait, else
ACP_DISPATCH_LOAD_WAIT, else 1800; --no-load-gate or ACP_DISPATCH_NO_LOAD_GATE=1 skips it; LW_* is scrubbed from its
environment except the knobs passed as flags). Then, under this shim's launch lock, the live count: `paseo ls -g
--background --label ade.via=acp-dispatch --json`, agents whose status is running or initializing; at LW_MAX_AGENTS
(default 14, 0 off) or more it waits inside the --load-wait budget and then exits 75 (`refused=agents`). Then
`paseo run --provider P/M --mode MODE --no-wait --json --title NAME --cwd DIR --label ade.via=acp-dispatch --label
ade.kind=KIND --label ade.name=NAME --label ade.lead=LEAD [--thinking EFFORT] -- PROMPT`, where PROMPT is one
paragraph naming the brief copy (`<out>/<name>-brief.md`, never written into the repo), the report path, and the
footer. The lock and the admit reservation are released once the new agent shows in that list (up to 10 s), so a
burst of launches cannot pass the cap together. A review-launch run holds its admit reservation (renewed) until it
ends: it is a `claude -p` process `paseo ls` cannot see.

Wait: `paseo wait ID [--timeout S] --json`, read by its status field, never its exit status: idle -> the report is
classified (0 DONE, 1 unfinished, 3 no report, 4 BLOCKED); timeout -> 124 (the agent keeps running: `paseo stop ID`
to end it); permission -> 4 with the pending permission names from `paseo inspect ID --json`; error -> 3. Without
--detach --no-wait the dispatch waits inline (`wait_timeout`: --wait-timeout, else --timeout + 300 s, 0 = none).
Nothing stops a Paseo agent at --timeout: the brief's time budget asks it to report first.

Contract (the same for these slices and for Claude Code Agent-tool sub-agents, which get the footer pasted):
    report   $OUT/<name>-report.md   first line `STATUS: working` or `BLOCKED: <question>`; last line `DONE`
                                     (optionally followed by one `AC_DONE:` verdict line)
    done     <report>.done            touched last; waiters watch this, never the report
    record   $OUT/jobs/<name>.json    paseo_agent_id, provider, mode, boundary, started, wait_timeout, argv, ...
    $OUT     ~/.local/state/bigteam/<task>/ (default adhoc-<date>) or --out; never the session scratchpad

--kind frontier keeps its admission (bin/agent_guard.py's identity policy, the estimate floor, the in-flight
reservation and the per-wave cap of the frontier allowance, docs/gates.md): a frontier model needs --kind frontier,
--role exec needs ACP_OPERATOR_APPROVED=frontier-exec, fable at --effort xhigh/max needs fable-xhigh, hermes needs
ACP_OPERATOR_APPROVED=hermes. Every kind is checked against route_agent's eligibility (route-override skips it).

Exit codes (dispatch, wait and check):
    0    report delivered and ends in DONE        1    report present but unfinished; still running
    2    usage or a refused launch                 3    no report (or a NO-REPORT: line)
    4    BLOCKED (first line, or a pending permission)
    5    pool unavailable before launch (headroom, wont-fit, in-flight reservation or cap): re-plan
    75   machine too hot to start (load-watch admit, or the agent cap): nothing launched, retry later
    77   tripwire (review-launch: a tool or read outside the boundary)   124  timed out waiting
Exit 0 is still not success: verify the outcome (diff, tests, the report's content).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import atexit
import fcntl
import json
import math
import os
